{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2588 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "ba46f7a12760de5543223b25d9f8f63e5c235548d3a67ae7dad7ee292e1165ce" :edb/db-before-t 2587 :edb/db-after-t 2588 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535900 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:12:23.527Z" 13194139535900 true] [17592186175881 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373340 13194139535900 true] [17592186175881 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373350 13194139535900 true] [17592186175881 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373354 13194139535900 true] [17592186175946 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373333 13194139535900 true] [17592186175946 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373347 13194139535900 true] [17592186373333 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373334 13194139535900 true] [17592186373333 1089 "q-118556" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373333 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535900 true] [17592186373333 1100 "The population $y(t)$ of chimpanzees in a Brazilian forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(1-\\frac{y}{500}),\\,y(0)=70,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible chimpanzee population?" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373333 1113 #uuid "bfb7dca1-926a-572e-ba91-5ebc76856166" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373333 1145 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(1-\\frac{y}{500}) \\\\  & =y(\\frac{500-y}{500}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{500}(500-y) \\\\  & =0.002y(500-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=500.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $500,$ and we conclude that the number of chimpanzees cannot exceed $500.$" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373335 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373336 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373337 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373338 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373339 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1041 "selection" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373337 13194139535900 true] [17592186373334 1110 #uuid "0c3a0e6e-e35f-584a-80a0-05c57473c470" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373335 1034 "700" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373335 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535900 true] [17592186373335 1111 #uuid "ce18df0d-d2e8-5300-a802-abf911acc97e" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373336 1034 "430" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535900 true] [17592186373336 1111 #uuid "9f16fa97-0187-5da6-ac08-b99d85756335" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373337 1034 "500" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373337 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535900 true] [17592186373337 1111 #uuid "a8d611c0-3f26-5ec6-abe8-af0f27483556" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373338 1034 "1\\,000" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535900 true] [17592186373338 1111 #uuid "e00b73ba-6d3f-5dbc-88a7-d1c4c0694d67" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373339 1034 "570" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373339 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535900 true] [17592186373339 1111 #uuid "213504b5-37c4-5932-992d-059063811f2a" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373340 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373341 13194139535900 true] [17592186373340 1089 "q-119854" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373340 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535900 true] [17592186373340 1100 "The rate of growth in the number of plants $P(t)$ infected with a pest in a certain land follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.5P-0.0025{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=5.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in months. For which value of $P$ is the number of plants infected with the pest growing at the fastest possible rate?" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373340 1113 #uuid "6a431b28-61ce-5f6e-a7e6-4c7a67f4a70c" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373340 1145 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.5P-0.0025{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.0025P(200-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=200.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $200,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 200=100.\n$$" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373342 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373343 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373344 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373345 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373346 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1041 "selection" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373344 13194139535900 true] [17592186373341 1110 #uuid "68614526-0b46-510e-a051-625b2bf9a76e" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373342 1034 "50" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535900 true] [17592186373342 1111 #uuid "6de42081-d