)\n\nFrom our equation, we see that $a=8000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $8000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8000=4000.\n$$" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373352 13194139535900 true] [17592186373351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373353 13194139535900 true] [17592186373351 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535900 true] [17592186373351 1041 "field-1" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373351 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373352 13194139535900 true] [17592186373351 1110 #uuid "12e41285-b22e-5a98-bd15-9b5059c5221b" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373352 1034 "4000" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535900 true] [17592186373352 1111 #uuid "e5650d47-4d89-573e-b606-9b3c79887688" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373353 1034 "8000" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535900 true] [17592186373353 1111 #uuid "36e3e12a-97af-5ac0-9fda-ef2bf5a6a9cc" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373354 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373355 13194139535900 true] [17592186373354 1089 "q-353490" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373354 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535900 true] [17592186373354 1100 "The number $P(t)$ of stores in a retail chain follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=6300P-7{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=50,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the number of stores growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373354 1113 #uuid "c7b7a1b4-7de9-54a7-9f4b-1f06a4d3bf67" 13194139535900 true] [17592186373354 1145 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/as